{"seq":35,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0783"},"reason":"Added a note: in English the low storey above the main cornice is usually called an 'attic' (attic storey); 'Attica'/Attika is the Latin/German form shared with the region around Athens, so 'attic' is accepted.","by":"provenance-research","sources":[{"url":"https://www.dictionary.com/browse/attic"},{"url":"https://www.dwds.de/wb/Attika"}],"changes":[{"field":"notesEn","old":"","new":"In English the low storey above the main cornice is usually called an attic or attic storey; Attica (German Attika) is the Latin form the term shares with the region around Athens, so \"attic\" counts too."},{"field":"notesDe","old":"","new":"Im Englischen heißt das niedrige Geschoss über dem Hauptgesims meist attic (attic storey); Attika ist die lateinische Form, die der Begriff mit der Landschaft um Athen teilt."},{"field":"notesRu","old":"","new":"По-английски низкий этаж над главным карнизом обычно называют attic (attic storey); «аттик» происходит от латинского Attica — так же называется область вокруг Афин."}],"hash":"7cf751e9bbd5","actor":{"kind":"agent","name":"provenance-research"},"run":"provenance-research-2026-10-23","chain":"596072cdee24da1d0044828ceaf71659c71ebb938ad7bbdb3a8d2d78a79df919"},
